    "body": "## Summary\n\nCommits 2+3 of ADR-029: the flex layout algorithm AND the viewport feature-class injection that unlocks its visible delta.\n\n**Landing both together** because Commit 2 alone is a *regression* on Wikipedia — the measured delta was +165px (worse), not −526px (predicted). The measurement discipline caught it before merge.\n\n## The two-stage measurement\n\nMeasured on Wikipedia at viewport 1774, `.mw-page-container-inner` (the grid container — the article sits directly below it):\n\n| Stage | y-coordinate | Delta vs baseline |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Baseline** (pre-ADR-029) | 585 | — |\n| **Commit 2 alone** (flex, no flip) | 750 | **+165 (regression)** |\n| **Commit 2 + Commit 3** (flex + flip) | **59** | **−526 (payoff)** |\n\nHeader height, same viewports:\n\n| Element | Before | Commit 2 | Commit 2+3 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `.vector-header-container` | — | 727 | **36** |\n| `.vector-header-start` | — | 711 | **5** |\n| `.vector-header-end` | — | 20 | 20 |\n\nThe article content finally appears **above the fold** — for the first time since the CSS-layout arc began at ADR-025.\n\n## Why Commit 2 alone was a regression\n\nWikipedia's Vector 2022 skin ships `<html class=\"... vector-feature-main-menu-pinned-disabled ...\">` when fetched without JS. A small inline `<script>` at page load flips that to `-enabled` at desktop viewports. Without the flip:\n\n- `.vector-main-menu-landmark` stays visible at **711px** (the mobile hamburger menu tree, rendered as vertical stacked blocks)\n- The header grows to 727px\n- Everything below shifts down by +165px\n\nWith the flip, `.vector-main-menu-landmark` hides via `display: none` (matching `.vector-feature-main-menu-pinned-enabled .vector-header-start .vector-main-menu-landmark`), and the header collapses to 36px.\n\n**The flex algorithm is correct in both cases** — unit tests pass 10/10 either way. The visible delta depends entirely on whether the landmark is hidden.\n\n## Commit 2: `layout_flex_children`\n\nSingle-line flex per ADR-029's scope:\n\n- `Display::Flex` / `Display::InlineFlex` dispatch in `layout_element`\n- **Direction**: `row` (default) | `column`\n- **`justify-content`**: `flex-start` | `flex-end` | `center` | `space-between` | `space-around` | `end`\n- **`align-items`**: `stretch` (default) | `flex-start` | `flex-end` | `center`\n- **Per-item**: `flex-grow`, `flex-shrink`, `flex-basis`\n- **Gap**: `gap` / `row-gap` / `column-gap`\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Dual-pass per child: natural layout at `(0,0)` for basis resolution, final layout at computed position/size\n2. Grow/shrink distribution: proportional to `grow` ratios or `shrink*basis` ratios\n3. Main-axis positioning per `justify-content`, with `space-between`/`space-around` computed as effective gap\n4. Cross-axis positioning per `align-items`\n\n## Commit 3: viewport feature-class flip\n\n`apply_viewport_feature_classes(doc, viewport)` in `render_pipeline.cpp`:\n\n- At **≥1120** (matching the grid `@media` breakpoint): rewrite `vector-feature-main-menu-pinned-disabled` → `-enabled` on `<html>`\n- At **<1120**: rewrite back to `-disabled` (idempotent round-trip; desktop→mobile→desktop stays correct)\n- Called at top of `RenderPipeline::relayout()`, **before** the cascade, so selector matching sees the flipped class\n- ~15 lines, honest mimicry of what Wikipedia's JS does\n\n**This is the correct architectural place for it:** the pipeline is the browser's \"JS substitute\" layer. When a page ships a JS-fixup that materially changes its visible layout, and we can do that fixup with a 15-line rule, doing it is honest — not a hack. It's what the user expects to see when they open Wikipedia in HoneyBee.\n\n## Three small bugs fixed during Commit 2's write-up\n\nThese are the kind of \"measure, ship, correct\" moments this arc's discipline surfaces:\n\n1. **`ComputedStyle::get` takes `const std::string&`** — my `get_prop` lambda signature used `std::string_view`; adjusted.\n2. **Explicit `flex-basis: 0` was being treated as natural size** — the \"parsed > 0\" guard broke `flex: 1 1 0` semantics (both children default to their content sizes, no free space to distribute, grow does nothing). Removed the guard; explicit basis including 0 is honored.\n3. **Flex test harness didn't zero body margin** — UA stylesheet has default `body { margin: 8px }`, so `x=0` assertions in tests were off by 8px. Prepended `body,html{margin:0;padding:0}` in `flex_prep`.\n\nAlso: initial `align-items` test used inline `style=\"height:100px\"` on child divs — which the test cascade doesn't parse, so the children were natural-height, and the cross-axis offset was 0. Rewritten to use natural content heights (nested divs; `fake_measure` yields 16px per line).\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before ADR-029 Commit 2: 379 cases, 1575 assertions\n- After Commit 2: **389 cases, 1628 assertions** (+10 / +53)\n- After Commit 3: **392 cases, 1637 assertions** (+3 / +9)\n- Full suite all pass, zero warnings\n\n## Verification checklist\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Flex algorithm: 10 unit tests (basis, grow, shrink, justify, align, direction, gap) | ✅ |\n| Flex: Wikipedia header places children side-by-side | ✅ |\n| Flex: `align-items: center` vertically centers `.mw-logo` | ✅ |\n| Flex: `flex-grow: 1` on `.vector-header-end` expands it | ✅ |\n| Feature-class flip: desktop flips disabled→enabled | ✅ |\n| Feature-class flip: mobile keeps disabled | ✅ |\n| Feature-class flip: desktop→mobile→desktop round-trip | ✅ |\n| **Wikipedia header collapses 727 → 36** | ✅ |\n| **`mw-page-container-inner` moves 750 → 59** | ✅ |\n| **Article content above the fold** | ✅ |\n| No regression to prior ADRs (grid, external CSS, nav, hover) | ✅ |\n| Full suite green | ✅ |\n\n## Deferred (per ADR-029)\n\n- `flex-wrap: wrap` (multi-line flex) — 0 visible impact at typical viewports\n- `row-reverse`, `column-reverse` — 0 uses\n- `align-self`, `align-content` — 0 uses\n- `order` — 0 uses\n- `inline-flex` participating in inline runs (treated as block-level flex)\n- Percentage cross-axis `flex-basis`\n\n## What the discipline earned\n\nThis is the first time the \"measure, predict, verify, correct\" pattern **prevented a regression from being merged** rather than correcting it in the record after:\n\n- Commit 2 alone would have shipped a −165px regression\n- The verification step caught it (single unit test file dump revealed it)\n- The diagnostic traced it to `<html class>` server-shipped state\n- Commit 3 fixed it in the correct layer (browser-side JS-substitute)\n- The two-stage measurement is now in the historical record\n\nSame discipline as ADR-028's post-hoc misdiagnosis correction — applied preventively for the first time.\n\nRefs #161\n",
